  "caption": "Quinn's mornings start like a rusty robot booting up: every joint creaks, and twisting to crack things loose does nothing.\n\nStiffness after rest is often ordinary, or linked to everyday arthritis. Joints tend to \"gel\" when still and loosen as you move. What matters most is how long it lasts.\n\nWhat can help: gentle movement early in the morning, a bit of warmth like a warm shower, breaking up long spells of sitting, and building strength around the joints. There's no need to force or crack joints to loosen them.\n\nSee your GP promptly if stiffness lasts more than an hour most days, joints look swollen, you feel unusually tired, or the small joints of both hands are affected.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
